                     <title>ʾAsmāt-prayer with a talismanic drawing.</title>
                     <quote xml:lang="gez"><hi rend="rubric">ወለመ፡ ገብሩ፡ ማዕተበ፡ ሰሎሞን፡ ፫ተ፡ ስሙ፡ ለአብ፡ ሙሩያል፡ ስሙ፡ ለወልድ፡ ምናቴር፡ ስሙ፡ ለመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ አብያቴር፡ ወለአመ፡ ተ 
                        <del rend="erasure" unit="chars" quantity="2"/> <gap reason="illegible" unit="chars" quantity="1"/> ተ<supplied reason="omitted">ገ</supplied>ብረ፡ በእሉ፡ አስማት፡ ይመርህዎ፡ መላእክት፡ ውስተ፡
                     መንግሥተ፡ ሰማያት፡ ከማሁ፡ ይምርሁኒ፡ ወያብኡኒ፡ ለገብርከ፡ ገብረ፡ እግዚአብሔር።</hi></quote>
                     <note>The text is written on a loose bifolio (<locus from="137a" to="137aa">137a–137aa</locus>) of smaller size and included between <locus target="#137"/> and the back board.
                        The names of the Persons of the Holy Trinity are very similar to those contained in <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1758Lefafa">Lǝfāfa ṣǝdq</ref>. 
                        The name of the supplicant, <persName role="other" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15247GabraEgzia">Gabra ʾƎgziʾabǝḥer</persName>, appears at the end of the prayer.</note>
